 # sds2-step-pipeline v5.5.3 — changes from the v4 candidate
 
+## v5.5w patch (agentjob sds2-weights-failures; same CLI, same outputs, new manifest fields)
+
+Weights (data-3 items "sds2 family weight" / "sds2 weight 5%"):
+- **Studs, rods, anchors and SDS2 bolt pieces are checked against SDS2's own piece weight** (`turned_brep`).
+  `special_solid` builds them from rings of mesh vertices or, failing that, a straight rod; nothing compared the result
+  with the piece weight. It wrote stud heads without shanks (EDWARDS AFB WS7/8 0.07 vs 1.04 lb), the first leg of
+  bent bars (Cats Rail RB1/2 0.18 vs 1.17 lb), curved rails as straight bars, and 7.039 headed studs at 3.47x (RCMS HS,
+  400 pieces). When the primitive is a guess, or more than 5 % off SDS2's weight, the piece's own closed B-rep is used
+  if it is within 15 % and closer (STERLING VIII RB3/4: 0.11x -> 1.0001x, all 101 bars exact).
+- **Ring detection no longer splits values on a .xxx5 boundary** (`_snap`; 0.4375 / 3.6875 were rounded into two keys).
+- **Square / hex rings stay polygons** (`_polygon_ring`): bolt heads / nuts with 4 or 6 vertices are the prism of
+  SDS2's own polygon, not a cylinder through its corners (+21 % on the head).
+- **Straight-rod stand-ins use the real diameter and length** (`rod_diameter`, `rod_length`): v5.4 used the table W
+  (RB3/4: W = 0.25) and L (the diameter on stud records). Still tagged `[approx: straight rod ...]`.
+- **Exact pieces whose B-rep is SDS2's own stock are no longer replaced by approximations** (`_stock_match`): a closed
+  B-rep outside the 0.6-1.6 weight gate is accepted when it equals the piece-table L x W x T (plates) or the section's
+  catalog lb/ft x L with table length x d x bf extents; the recorded weight is then the outlier
+  (`weight_check.sds2_weight_outliers`, kept out of the ratio). processing-Ted L8x8x3/4: catalog 1,556 lb, B-rep
+  1,563, recorded 4,000; AGRANCLISSEMENT 254S89-144M studs: record 7.53 lb/ft, B-rep 3.71 (v5.4 wrote a 15.9x profile).
+- **Weight tally split by geometry source**: `weight_check.by_source.{exact,built,standin}` and the same parts in every
+  `by_family` entry (`exact` = SDS2's own piece B-rep, `built` = untagged solids the converter built, `standin` =
+  tagged approximations), plus `weight_check.turned_brep`.
+- **Bent-plate fallback no longer hangs on large rings** (`BENT_DROP_BUDGET`; Cardinal Misc_job 7.135: > 45 min ->
+  212 s) and **gross fallbacks are gated at 10x / +50 lb** too (the 1,000-lb floor let MOUNTAIN VIEW BLDG#B-G 7.433
+  write 300 BPL10GAx83 3/16 at 206 lb each vs SDS2's 14.0 lb; such pieces get the piece-table slab stand-in).
+
+Stage-2 failures (data-3 item "sds2 stage 2 failure", 68 jobs on members-only stage 1):
+- **`batch/run_batch.parse_log` reads the last read-back block** (the fleet worker loads it from this zip). With
+  `--verify`, a read-back repair pass re-converts and re-verifies; the fleet judged the first, pre-repair block. 39
+  jobs fell back to stage 1 as `invalid_solids`; 31 of their final STEPs were within the limit (GREAT OAKS 7.132: 13,606
+  of 13,626 valid before the repair, 13,626 of 13,626 after).
+- **The repair pass can leave out instances of parts that failed the assembly check** (and flat-mode exact parts):
+  they went out as placed copies before `DROP_LABELS` was consulted, so solids that stay invalid as placed copies were
+  written again on the last pass (CCJ 7.132 x5, POLICE HEADQUARTERS 7.135, BAHAMAR BLDG#40 7.135: 46-256 invalid).
+  They are now dropped and reported (`exact_solid_invalid_at_placement`).
+- **Job folders without the piece table (`subm/subm_idx`)** convert (21 data-3 jobs; FileNotFoundError before):
+  members as tagged envelopes / joist stand-ins, SDS2 bolt records as usual, and where `subm/` still holds the piece
+  files (BOSK_E 8.010, TATTIER 7.312, RCMS 7.039 x2) each piece the member files place is written from SDS2's stored
+  B-rep (`brep_unindexed`: closed solids only, decoded holes cut), tagged `[unindexed: ...]` because its name, section
+  and weight are not in the job. Manifest: `counts.piece_table_absent`, `counts.subm_piece_files`, stand-in type
+  `unindexed_brep`; never class 1. `instances._is_71` / `_is_70` take the layout from `main/jsetup` when there is no
+  `subm_idx`.
+- **Bolt-derived holes skip parts with a void bounding box** (Nantucket JOB 29MAY14 7.312: `Standard_ConstructionError:
+  Bnd_Box is void` failed the whole stage 2).
+
+ValueErrors (data-3 item "valueerror"):
+- **`sparse_layout` tolerates stale member records** (same change as the SDS2 fixer's v5.5.4 draft, `rel554`): 15-027
+  CSU 7.312 has 810 COLUMN records with NaN end points among 10,452.
+- **The documented 7.243 layout is a sparse fallback** (module docstring, validated on 50_Binney): 100_Binney_Slab_Job
+  (7.243, three MISC members, no work-point key match) failed with `member work points not found`.
+
 ## v5.5.3 (v5.5.0 + three fixes, released together; same CLI)
 
 Released as one version (owner: avoid three re-run waves). The fixes are listed as 5.5.1, 5.5.2 and 5.5.3.
